{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019","id":1556317,"title":"Notes Towards A \u2018Lone Star By Night\u2019","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-07T15:29:03-08:00","id":1556317,"title":"Notes Towards A \u2018Lone Star By Night\u2019","content":"<i>\u201cTexas is the reason/that the president\u2019s dead\u201d<br /> -The Misfits, \u2018Bullet\u2019</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s often observed that classic White Wolf lore was very western centric, particularly the United States, particularly the Midwest, Northeast, &amp; West Coast. This has created a situation where some of the largest cities in the US today, see Houston or Dallas, have barely anything to go on about them.<br /> <br /> My hopes with this project is to sketch out the outlines of what a Texas vampire setting might look like with you all. I enjoy trying to build in verisimilitude for my games and big open areas like these are begging to be filled in. I invite everyone to share whatever thoughts come to mind. I\u2019m not from Texas or the South and I\u2019m not a historian of the region, so my additions will be the best I can put together based on what I do know.<br /> <br /> Additional Disclaimer: I\u2019m sure some canon information does exist and could be useful to build on but I\u2019m largely treating this as a blank state, using the general knowledge of the setting we have from 1e/2e as my template <br /> <br /> Now, beginning in no particular order, I\u2019m going to through out a number of spit ball ideas. I may add the first drama of a historical sketch later as well:<br /> <br /> <b>Brainstorm </b><br /> <br /> \u2022For potential modern settings I\u2019ll include ideas both for a hypothetical 1990s start date and a contemporaneous 2020s start date <br /> <br /> \u2022I don\u2019t have the strongest feeling for what distinguishes the notable Texan cities but I think any setting guide probably needs to touch on the Texas Triangle (Dallas-Fort Worth, Houston, Antonio), Austin, El Paso, the Rio Grande, Hill Country, Texarkana, North Texas/Panhandle, West Texas, &amp; Gulf Coast<br /> <br /> \u2022A vibes based reading of three Texan cities:<br /> -Dallas (I see Dallas having the most classic Ventrue environment; big business, finance, etc; but with a bit of a more modern feel, the 80s boom and tech industry in mind; I imagine a relatively young Camarilla Ventrue prince whose stuck in the mode of 80s finance guy trying to keep a palatable face on the real power players who all cut their teeth in the 19th century or older, some of whom definitely have Dallas-the show style affectations)<br /> -Houston (Houston I see as doing away with the polite fictions of Dallas, instead having a Brujah Prince, probably the oldest in the state, who openly runs the city like a temple to blood and oil; if you play the game and are on the right side, it can be very comfortable and secure, but the rulers of Houston have little patience for those who would rock the boat)<br /> -Austin (I see Austin having a Toresdor prince, and being the city with a significant Anarch influence, the Prince maintaining a libertine posture and relatively lax enforcement of the traditions in an effort to keep the Texan Anarchs fat &amp; lazy/inside the tent pissing out-sort of vibe)<br /> <br /> \u2022I think a significant section could be dedicated to the vast swaths of Suburbia where Autarkis, Thin-Bloods, Caitiff, &amp; Nomads can all maintain carved out fiefdoms in new developments, condos, and strip malls <br /> <br /> \u2022I see a major element of the Texas Sabbat taking inspiration from Texas Chainsaw Massacre and Rob Zombie movies. With isolated revenant enclaves/safehouses modeled after TCM &amp; House of a 1,000 Corpses and nomads who are a mix of Near Dark &amp; the Devil\u2019s Rejects<br /> <br /> \u2022A subculture of hunters that take more influence from the post-70s evangelical movement than the Catholic Church, operating out of strip mall churches and blending into backroads, trailer parks, and cookie cutter suburbs<br /> <br /> \u2022Some sort of commentary on the rise of the Sun Belt from the 1970s onward, perhaps with a new breed of young Camarilla princes merging alongside the cities of the region, a sort of triangulation between the old blood and the Rust Belt princes of the Midwest &amp; Northeast who gained so much influence in the late 19th through mid-20th century <br /> -Maybe tie this to the LBJ years and his clique\u2019s national influence to tentpole this transition period before having the figurehead of this be more Bush Oil Cowboy/Safari Club inspired <br /> <br /> \u2022Use of the Dallas/Austin counter culture of the 1980s &amp; 90s as a breeding ground for local anarch tendencies (see the history behind: Bill Hicks, Alex Jones, Matthew McConaughey, Linklater, \u201cSlacker\u201d, MDMA, the Dallas Tech Boom, etc.)<br /> <br /> \u2022Any version of this project that uses the 90s as a starting point is going to have to touch on the militia movement as well, perhaps using it as inspiration for Anarchs, Sabbat, and/or Hunters<br /> <br /> \u2022You also need some kind of Ross Perot reference in there for sure<br /> <br /> \u2022You also need to have some significant writing about Texas\u2019 relationship with Mexico but that also touches on addressing Mexico\u2019s place in the World of Darkness which goes beyond the scope of this post, but is definitely worth its own thread <br /> <br /> Non-Exhaustive List of Potential Inspirations<br /> \u2022Westerns (et. all)<br /> \u2022Near Dark<br /> \u2022Texas Chainsaw Massacre<br /> \u2022Rob Zombie movies (esp: House of 1,000 Corpses, The Devil\u2019s Rejects)<br /> \u2022No Country For Old Men (&amp; Corman McCarthy in general)<br /> \u2022Breaking Bad, Better Call Saul (more southwest in general than Texas I know, but I\u2019m counting \u2018em)<br /> \u2022The Righteous Gemstones &amp; Nashville (also not Texas obviously but useful viewing IMO)<br /> \u2022Slacker<br /> \u2022Any biography of LBJ<br /> \u2022Dallas (the TV Series)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T21:22:27-08:00","id":1556331,"title":"","content":"Random stuff that could or should offer inspiration and ideas:<br /> <br /> Empire of the Summer Moon, the nonfiction book about the Comanche.<br /> <br /> The TV series Halt and Catch Fire, especially the first two seasons which focus on the &quot;Silicon Prairie&quot; of the DFW area in the 80s.<br /> <br /> The Getaway (1972)<br /> Rolling Thunder (1977)<br /> Dazed and Confused (1993)<br /> Lone Star (1996)<br /> Office Space (1999)<br /> Bubba Ho-Tep (2002)<br /> Friday Night Lights (2004), especially for understanding the state's obsession with high school and college football <br /> The Iron Claw (2023)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T21:35:11-08:00","id":1556332,"title":"","content":"Ooh Halt &amp; Catch Fire is a great pull, I wish I\u2019d remembered that. That whole Silicon Prairie vibe, as well as being the location of the regional Federal Reserve bank and one of the financial hubs of the Oil Boom is part of why the image I had for Dallas was the sort of \u201cGordon Gecko of the South\u201d Camarilla Ventrue style domain. A bit too shiny, a bit greasy, a bit too eager to prove that everything\u2019s running smoothly while meanwhile the actual powers that be call the shots behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> Friday Night Lights is one I would never have thought of at first but is a good catch too. If California has surf vampires, then Texas, or the southeast more broadly, definitely needs small town/football vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T09:48:14-08:00","id":1556345,"title":"","content":"Texas is an extremely big region to cover. Texas has always been a hybrid between a &quot;southern&quot; and &quot;western&quot; state, and the DFW area seems to have a strong midwestern influence. It is really lots of different regions, more than most states. What combines it together is a strong state culture that prides itself on the Texan War of Independence and its existence as a separate republic for a decade.<br /> <br /> A major reason why LBJ was so powerful in the Senate was that he was the conduit between his fellow Democrats and the Texas oil money that fueled a lot of campaigns in other states. There's just a lot of political influence to be gained from that. That's probably why Meerlinda, the Tremere Councilor for North America, is based in Dallas, Texas. John Diamond (Pontifex for Commerce based in Bridgeport, CT) and Peter Dorfman (Pontifex for Politics in Washington, DC) may be responsible for Tremere influence there for North America, but they all report directly to her.<br /> <br /> The US territorial Pontifexes are organized into Eastern, Central, and Western regions. Other than the US Western Pontifex (Abe Powell) being based in Sacramento, I don't know where the other two are based. I can't find them in a (very quick) perusal of the clanbooks, and I don't believe they're mentioned in any canon By Night sourcebook. However, I imagine Texas falls under the US Central Pontifex. Regardless of where it is located (I would probably place it in St Louis as a convenient place), whatever Meerlinda wants to happen in the Texan chantries probably gets done without question.<br /> <br /> Because of the state's cattle and cotton economy, wide swaths of the state are probably &quot;controlled&quot; by Lupines. Not to mention that the resource extraction economy will attract a lot of attention from them. While short distances between major cities are probably OK to travel with the modern highway system at night (most of the time), that would not have been the case historically. And entire regions of Texas are probably off limits to vampires because of Lupine activity. Any cowboy or small town football vampires in Texas better be Gangrel and keep close to the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Texas Chainsaw Massacre inspired Bratovitch revenants are one of the few spots the Sabbat can somewhat safely move between when trying to cross the state, but the vaunted &quot;lupine hunters&quot; of the Bratovitch likely keep their head down and only have a few trophies based on isolated Ronin, Lost Cubs, and Lunatics that they can safely ambush on rare occasions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:46:47-08:00","id":1556358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556345#post1556345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Texas is an extremely big region to cover. Texas has always been a hybrid between a &quot;southern&quot; and &quot;western&quot; state, and the DFW area seems to have a strong midwestern influence. It is really lots of different regions, more than most states. What combines it together is a strong state culture that prides itself on the Texan War of Independence and its existence as a separate republic for a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the sheer size of Texas makes it somewhat tricky to sketch out or make any broad generalizations to be sure. In a way it\u2019s as much a region as any New England or Southeast by night would have to be. One of the reasons I wanted to think about how to sketch in Texas, aside from it having two of the largest metropolitan areas in the US, was because of the way it serves as a bridge/crossroads between the Southeast/Southwest/Midwest/Northern Mexico and thus could hopefully be built off of for explorations of those regions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556345#post1556345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major reason why LBJ was so powerful in the Senate was that he was the conduit between his fellow Democrats and the Texas oil money that fueled a lot of campaigns in other states. There's just a lot of political influence to be gained from that. That's probably why Meerlinda, the Tremere Councilor for North America, is based in Dallas, Texas. John Diamond (Pontifex for Commerce based in Bridgeport, CT) and Peter Dorfman (Pontifex for Politics in Washington, DC) may be responsible for Tremere influence there for North America, but they all report directly to her.<br /> <br /> The US territorial Pontifexes are organized into Eastern, Central, and Western regions. Other than the US Western Pontifex (Abe Powell) being based in Sacramento, I don't know where the other two are based. I can't find them in a (very quick) perusal of the clanbooks, and I don't believe they're mentioned in any canon By Night sourcebook. However, I imagine Texas falls under the US Central Pontifex. Regardless of where it is located (I would probably place it in St Louis as a convenient place), whatever Meerlinda wants to happen in the Texan chantries probably gets done without question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had half-remembered that Meerlinda was stationed in Texas, thanks for reminding us of this. In that vein, with a major Tremere hub in Texas, part of me is tempted to use that to do a sort of Cyclonopedia (by Reza Negarestani) style thing. For those not familiar, Cyclonopedia is a work of CCRU-inflected \u201ctheory fiction\u201d, a sort of creative pseudo-non-fiction or ARG kinda work that posits Oil as a psuedo-sentient entity which is actively using human beings to foster its own ends of recreating a planet-state resembling the ultra-tropical period of its dinosaur-composition lived. It\u2019s kind of cybernetics mixed with the Living Oil subplot from the X-Files. I think it\u2019s probably too esoteric to be a central plot point but maybe a sort of background mystery that could serve as a crossover for Vampire/Werewolf/Mage, reminiscent of the White Worm in Vienna or the Tumor under NYC.<br /> <br /> I do think the LBJ years are so juicy that you\u2019ve gotta put some threads onto that. The conspiratorial themes that the Tremere have running through them and LBJ\u2019s proximity to the JFK assassination mythos makes it a cinch IMO. Plus you\u2019ve got Houston and NASA that you can play around with, as well as the aforementioned connections to the Oil Industry and all of its sprawly connections. You don\u2019t necessarily need to go full Oliver Stone\u2019s JFK/Nixon unless folks want to, but any Lone Star by Night should probably have nods in that directions for STs to play with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556345#post1556345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of the state's cattle and cotton economy, wide swaths of the state are probably &quot;controlled&quot; by Lupines. Not to mention that the resource extraction economy will attract a lot of attention from them. While short distances between major cities are probably OK to travel with the modern highway system at night (most of the time), that would not have been the case historically. And entire regions of Texas are probably off limits to vampires because of Lupine activity. Any cowboy or small town football vampires in Texas better be Gangrel and keep close to the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Texas Chainsaw Massacre inspired Bratovitch revenants are one of the few spots the Sabbat can somewhat safely move between when trying to cross the state, but the vaunted &quot;lupine hunters&quot; of the Bratovitch likely keep their head down and only have a few trophies based on isolated Ronin, Lost Cubs, and Lunatics that they can safely ambush on rare occasions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree, Texas for vampires having a sort of \u201cislands of light\u201d vibe makes sense to me. I see the Gangrel being pretty important throughout the whole Southwest as Coyotes and Messengers, so maybe some unique local institution to represent that like a particular kind of Gather would be useful.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got Camarilla strongholds, Sabbat safehouses, and maybe a handful of small Autarkis/Clanless enclaves dotted throughout the suburban sprawl and a handful of small towns with nomads circulating along a few semi-secure routes in between vast swaths of rural zone under lupine influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":".  Misspelled the author of cyclonopedia\u2019s name 12-08-2025, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T15:57:46-08:00","id":1556371,"title":"","content":"I have long wished that Vampire had done a couple of regional sourcebooks which only did broad overviews of the area while primarily focused on talking about that region's specific literary traditions and how to apply them to Vampire. The Deep South and Southern Gothic, New England and stuff like Hawthorne, Lovecraft, and King, and the Southwest and Westerns.<br /> <br /> In the case of Texas, it also gets to do Southern Gothic, primarily in the east. Robert E Howard did several horror stories set in the ArkLaTex region where the three states meet, with &quot;Pigeons from Hell&quot; being the most famous.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of Tejano folklore, including horror stories, that would probably be suitable influences for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T15:46:31-08:00","id":1556444,"title":"","content":"While only a sometime guest of the Lone Star State, I\u2019m happy to jump in with some thoughts - one element I recall from the Anarch Free States threads curated by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> a while back is that Tara of Clan Brujah, the incumbent Anarch Baron/Camarilla Prince of San Diego, got her start in Texas and appears to have pulled a significant number of vampire with her as she decamped for California (Which likely affected Brujah numbers in the state).<br /> <br /> I also recall that Vannevar Thomas, future Prince of San Francisco, was accepted into the Camarilla by Texas Kindred (It\u2019s in PRINCE OF THE CITY) and was originally sent West to make claims in Gold Rush California on behalf of the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> Whilst these events were three quarters of a century and change apart, they do suggest that ties between California and Texas vampires could be historically-significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T15:53:07-08:00","id":1556445,"title":"","content":"Going by the usual ratios, with a population of 31,290,831 mortals the Great State of Texas could support as many as:-<br /> <br /> - 313 Kindred (1/100,000 \u2018Camarilla\u2019 ratio)<br /> <br /> - 616 Cainites (1/50,000 \u2018Sabbat\u2019 ratio)<br /> <br /> - 156 Garou (1/500,000 ratio).<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course these are a hypothetical maximum and the exact figures may differ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T15:56:12-08:00","id":1556446,"title":"","content":"A quick look at the White Wolf Wiki suggests that there were no major caerns in what we would now call Texas in the days of CROATAN SONG: also, El Paso is the domain of a Sabbat Bishop called Jose Chavez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T22:57:49-08:00","id":1556462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556445#post1556445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course these are a hypothetical maximum and the exact figures may differ.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla and Sabbat numbers are always based on the metropolitan urban area. So one should never include the rural population as the basis for vampires. Even though the suburban population is counted as part of the metro area, it's also always mentioned that the typical American suburb is NOT conducive to vampires. It lacks the high population density that lends itself to anonymity, high crime rates, and active nightlife that attracts modern vampires to the city. Instead, there's an implicit assumption that suburbanites commute to the urban core for the nightlife so that they contribute to the vampire population requirements, even though the suburbs themselves are usually not amenable to vampire populations.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there will always be some Gangrel or other nomadic vampire in the rural areas, but they will be much lower than the typical ratios and most often are already factored in by the metro area populations/sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> As for the Garou, I have never found that ratio to be helpful. Unlike vampires, Garou population is not dependent on the number of available humans because Garou do not feed on humans. Instead, Garou population is usually based around kinfolk populations that don't have direct correlation to the normal human population. This is very much in ST fiat situations. The Yukon Territory of Canada has less than 50,000 people. So per that ratio, there may not even be one Garou. Yet there's around 5000 wild wolves throughout the entire territory, and most people would accept that there should be very high numbers of Wendigo kinfolk and likely other tribal kinfolk as well. There's probably a lot more Garou there than, say, in Vermont which has a population of almost 650,000 or even Massachusetts which is over 7 million. A flat 500,000 people : 1 Garou will always lead to much more Garou in urban areas than rural areas, which is exactly the opposite of what it should be.<br /> <br /> Instead, I work backwards based on how many caerns I think should be in that territory. Research the geography and local legends. Assign the number of caerns and their rankings, and then assign the number of Garou appropriate for those caerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T05:31:26-08:00","id":1556468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019#post1556317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u2022A subculture of hunters that take more influence from the post-70s evangelical movement than the Catholic Church, operating out of strip mall churches and blending into backroads, trailer parks, and cookie cutter suburbs</div> </div> </div> </div>My go-to for such a thing is The Long Night faction from the 1st edition of Hunter: The Vigil. In the 80s and 90s, such a thing would likely be held together and spread via some mix of Jack Chick-style comic tracts warning of monsters and demons that walk among us, small time revivalist preachers who appear on local AM radio and UHF stations on early Sunday morning, and late night local talk radio call in hosts who are likely to talk about UFOs and missing persons cases as they are vampires or Satanic cults. (Probably never anyone with a national audience like the major televangelists or political pundits or shock jocks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T07:05:53-08:00","id":1556470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556462#post1556462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Camarilla and Sabbat numbers are always based on the metropolitan urban area. So one should never include the rural population as the basis for vampires. Even though the suburban population is counted as part of the metro area, it's also always mentioned that the typical American suburb is NOT conducive to vampires. It lacks the high population density that lends itself to anonymity, high crime rates, and active nightlife that attracts modern vampires to the city. Instead, there's an implicit assumption that suburbanites commute to the urban core for the nightlife so that they contribute to the vampire population requirements, even though the suburbs themselves are usually not amenable to vampire populations.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there will always be some Gangrel or other nomadic vampire in the rural areas, but they will be much lower than the typical ratios and most often are already factored in by the metro area populations/sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> As for the Garou, I have never found that ratio to be helpful. Unlike vampires, Garou population is not dependent on the number of available humans because Garou do not feed on humans. Instead, Garou population is usually based around kinfolk populations that don't have direct correlation to the normal human population. This is very much in ST fiat situations. The Yukon Territory of Canada has less than 50,000 people. So per that ratio, there may not even be one Garou. Yet there's around 5000 wild wolves throughout the entire territory, and most people would accept that there should be very high numbers of Wendigo kinfolk and likely other tribal kinfolk as well. There's probably a lot more Garou there than, say, in Vermont which has a population of almost 650,000 or even Massachusetts which is over 7 million. A flat 500,000 people : 1 Garou will always lead to much more Garou in urban areas than rural areas, which is exactly the opposite of what it should be.<br /> <br /> Instead, I work backwards based on how many caerns I think should be in that territory. Research the geography and local legends. Assign the number of caerns and their rankings, and then assign the number of Garou appropriate for those caerns.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a perfectly sensible \u2018in depth\u2019 approach, but is somewhat unhelpful when it comes coming up with off-the-cuff estimates (and I must admit to attempting nothing more useful than that).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wonder if one could work out a way to make the 1/500,000 ratio work a little more convincingly (Possibly something to do with human population density - the less dense the population, the fewer werewolves - so past a certain number of people per square mile subtract a certain percentage from the possible total of werewolves?).<br /> <br /> Sadly Mathematics and Statistics are not my strength.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T18:31:30-08:00","id":1556492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556462#post1556462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla and Sabbat numbers are always based on the metropolitan urban area. So one should never include the rural population as the basis for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not reading the whole thread yet, but I want to say something here.<br /> <br /> I do think rural population should be counted for determining vampires. Even if they won't <i>house</i> vampires, they're still available targets, especially when they also commute to urban areas for one reason or another, and they help define how much infrastructure is there (even if not high quality) in the rural area, which also helps vampires if/when they wander around.<br /> <br /> As far as statistics goes, as small as those factors are, they add up, and just adding this population as normal is a good enough compromise, if not the actual assumption of this ratio to begin with.<br /> <br /> But remember to adjust those ratios to the intended effect, and that the usual numbers are not for each sect, in theory it would be 1:100.000 overall, not for the Camarilla alone. Even then, you can run with anything between 1:10.000 and 1:200.000 depending on how much you want the state to be seen as empty or crowded (those being extremes, beyond them Kindred society shouldn't work as is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556470#post1556470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly Mathematics and Statistics are not my strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're mine, but they're not your friends here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s point is that tying the Garou to the population in any way, shape or form is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Your best take for Garou is to not establish an overall population at all. Instead, define the main sects in the area, those with the biggest Caerns or overall impact, and describe them with whatever you need.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Garou numbers fluctuate far more than any other splat. As rare as they are at any given moment, there's always Garou being born, Garou going through the First Change and Garou dying. If they had a reasonable life expectancy, it's hard to say if they wouldn't overtake every other splat in numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T18:38:07-08:00","id":1556493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>No One of Consequence</b><br /> I have long wished that Vampire had done a couple of regional sourcebooks which only did broad overviews of the area while primarily focused on talking about that region's specific literary traditions and how to apply them to Vampire. The Deep South and Southern Gothic, New England and stuff like Hawthorne, Lovecraft, and King, and the Southwest and Westerns.<br /> <br /> In the case of Texas, it also gets to do Southern Gothic, primarily in the east. Robert E Howard did several horror stories set in the ArkLaTex region where the three states meet, with &quot;Pigeons from Hell&quot; being the most famous.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of Tejano folklore, including horror stories, that would probably be suitable influences for this. </div> </div> </div>I also think that regional source books or just regional worldbuilding in general would be really helpful in general and that\u2019s a big part of what inspired this project/thread for me. I had forgotten that Howard was a Texan too but his style of writing is definitely something that would be useful to look at. Honestly I might spend some time this weekend looking on Anna\u2019s Archive to see if there\u2019s any good lit crit dedicated to Texas literature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Atticus Cleanclaw</b><br /> <br /> Whilst these events were three quarters of a century and change apart, they do suggest that ties between California and Texas vampires could be historically-significant.\u200b </div> </div> </div>That wouldn\u2019t surprise me at all tbh. California history is hugely influenced by not just Midwestern but also Southern immigration, which will inevitably include Texas. Particularly with the two being sister states of the Oil &amp; Sun Belts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T18:52:47-08:00","id":1556494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556468#post1556468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My go-to for such a thing is The Long Night faction from the 1st edition of Hunter: The Vigil. In the 80s and 90s, such a thing would likely be held together and spread via some mix of Jack Chick-style comic tracts warning of monsters and demons that walk among us, small time revivalist preachers who appear on local AM radio and UHF stations on early Sunday morning, and late night local talk radio call in hosts who are likely to talk about UFOs and missing persons cases as they are vampires or Satanic cults. (Probably never anyone with a national audience like the major televangelists or political pundits or shock jocks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh 100% that\u2019s totally one of the vibes I\u2019d want to be pulling from here. Especially if one assumes an early 90s starting date, no sourcebook on Texas would have been complete without such references. Honestly, as an aside, this could also be an opportunity to explore why some vampires might dabble in a little light diabolism, or even just the aesthetics of it, because of their cultural origins.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also tempted to see if I can work up an Alex Jones-expy and fit in the urban legend that he and Bill Hicks are the same person. Probably a bit lazy too do that directly, you\u2019d have to find some sort of extra hook, but I\u2019d bet if that region book got made back in the day you might\u2019ve seen just such a character. <br /> <br /> Honestly a group like the Long Night would be so useful for all across the US (but esp the Southeast, Southwest, &amp; Midwest that it might be worth its own dedicated thread at some point.<br /> <br /> I should also look up how involved Texas was in the cattle mutilation phenomenon. IIRC the first \u2018canonical\u2019 incident was either in Arizona or Wyoming, but given that reports cropped up across the southwest &amp; Midwest I\u2019d be surprised if Texas didn\u2019t have a part. It\u2019s not purely a Texan phenomenon either but this is the era of Bill Cooper and Dulce Base/Black Triangle mythology (in the southwest in particular) so while I usually associate such subject matter more with Mage or Changeling\u2019s milieu it could add some good background flavor. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T19:17:48-08:00","id":1556497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556493#post1556493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that regional source books or just regional worldbuilding in general would be really helpful in general and that\u2019s a big part of what inspired this project/thread for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that overall it's hard to make good regional books/worldbuilding without local writers, and finding local writers is hard. Ask anyone who actually live in the places depicted in almost every <i>By Night</i> or <i>Rage Across</i> book.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I don't forgive WoD for those terrible books is that at the time <i>Shadowrun</i> was doing exactly that: <i>German: Deutschland in den Schatten</i> (in English something like &quot;Germany in the Shadows&quot;, but translated just as <i>Germany Sourcebook</i>) was literally given to the local fanbase for them to write, and it was one of the best area books for an RPG.<br /> <br /> So while I think more such books would be nice, I don't think White Wolf at the time should have done them even more than they already did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T11:26:14-08:00","id":1556525,"title":"","content":"Handing regional sourcebooks to local fans would be the ideal, but it does present certain practical difficulties of it\u2019s own (For example, Germany is a country with a whole nation to draw on, but what if there simply aren\u2019t very many fans of the game in a potentially-interesting setting?) and rather dismisses the possibility that even a flawed resource may be interesting enough to attract the very fans who might improve on it.<br /> <br /> On a more cynical note, there\u2019s never a guarantee that fans will be able to equal their local enthusiasm with their writing skills!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I do, however, agree that a regional sourcebook will generally benefit when the authors consult local fans and that this will definitely be of help to non-resident authors trying to channel some serious Local Character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:17:28-08:00","id":1556526,"title":"","content":"Speaking of local character, it struck me that whilst a \u2018Lone Star By Night\u2019 sourcebook might be a trifle too ambitious, a city sourcebook in the classic VAMPIRE style might be more bite sized (No pun intended).<br /> <br /> When picking a suitable focus for such an effort, my suggestion would be to look up lists of the biggest cities in any given area and then look up the most dangerous cities in the said area- because logically a city where a population of vampires prosper is one where the blood flows most freely in the streets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on some internet research Dallas (13), Houston (1), San Antonio (6) and Corpus Christi (7) all appear on the list of the most populous settlements in Texas AND on a list of the least safe cities in the Lone Star State (Dallas, Houston and San Antonio all appear on the list of the most populous metro areas to boot.<br /> <br /> From this shortlist, San Antonio particularly leaps out (Based partly on it\u2019s strong association with the birth of Texas, but also because it\u2019s Spanish name helps remind us that the roots of Texas lie outside the English-speaking world), if only because one can readily imagine it\u2019s association with all the fame of the Alamo making it an excellent \u2018neutral ground\u2019 for meetings between vampires even before the city itself became populous enough to support a substantive resident population of Kindred (and tensions stemming from the clashes likely to ensue when a local vampire population grows large enough to exert Praxis over formerly-neutral ground could lend interest to local politics).<br /> <br /> Also, the title \u2018GRINDHOUSE ALAMO\u2019 suggests itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Spelling errors 12-16-2025, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:19:50-08:00","id":1556528,"title":"","content":"Heck, it has just struck me that making San Antonio a city more or less run by a council of primogen because even Texas vampires can\u2019t agree who gets to claim Praxis over the Alamo might be an interesting local wrinkle to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:27:13-08:00","id":1556532,"title":"","content":"N.B. According to my estimates, the cities on the shortlist above would have roughly the following number of vampires:-<br /> <br /> - Dallas: 13-26<br /> <br /> - Houston: 24-48<br /> <br /> - San Antonio: 15-30<br /> <br /> - Corpus Christi: 3-6 (Good size for a PC coterie to call their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T14:54:46-08:00","id":1556538,"title":"","content":"If you are going to do one city in Texas, it should be the Dallas/Forth Worth metroplex. While it's technically two different cities, it comprises one single urban area. It would be silly to do Dallas, but not include Fort Worth. I can't tell if by &quot;Dallas&quot; you mean just that city or mean to include Fort Worth with it. DFW is, in fact, slightly bigger than the metro Houston area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T17:51:21-08:00","id":1556546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556525#post1556525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Handing regional sourcebooks to local fans would be the ideal<br /> <br /> I do, however, agree that a regional sourcebook will generally benefit when the authors consult local fans and that this will definitely be of help to non-resident authors trying to channel some serious Local Character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ideal isn't the first, it's the last part. Better yet, is for you to pay a consultant or two that can help you navigate the process.<br /> <br /> It's what Onyx Path did on lots of books, and quite standard fare nowadays.<br /> <br /> But don't underestimate how obnoxious and harmful an ignorant take on the place can be, even if well written. Especially because a lot of people won't really ever go beyond whatever you write, and they do expect a company to know what they're talking about. So you should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556526#post1556526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of local character, it struck me that whilst a \u2018Lone Star By Night\u2019 sourcebook might be a trifle too ambitious, a city sourcebook in the classic VAMPIRE style might be mkre bite sized (No pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem being, it doesn't really helps with most splats.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Mage strongly need a broader take even when you're talking the most urbanite types. Changeling, Hunter, Demon and Mummy can work within a single city, but will often have to look outward, and sometimes this will happen quite soon. Only Vampire and Wraith really work confined to a given city in a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T06:15:57-08:00","id":1556711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556538#post1556538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going to do one city in Texas, it should be the Dallas/Forth Worth metroplex. While it's technically two different cities, it comprises one single urban area. It would be silly to do Dallas, but not include Fort Worth. I can't tell if by &quot;Dallas&quot; you mean just that city or mean to include Fort Worth with it. DFW is, in fact, slightly bigger than the metro Houston area.</div> </div> </div> </div> I admit to having quoted directly from Wikipedia and elsewhere, so it could be either: one must also agree that Dallas/Fort Worth has a strong claim to be THE Big City when it comes to Texas, hence one of the most logical settings for a local sourcebook.<br /> <br /> The only major quibble I can list against the notion is that Dallas/Fort Worth doesn\u2019t suggest a title half as fun as \u2018ALAMO GRINDHOUSE\u2019 (No, I was right the first time, \u2018GRINDHOUSE ALAMO\u2019 just looks better): I\u2019m also a little in love with the idea of using the whole sourcebook to bring to life the old joke that Texas could never be split into separate states (Annexation treaty or no) because nobody could decide who gets the Alamo.<br /> <br /> Also, it should be said that I\u2019ve actually visited San Antonio twice and have friendly memories of the place, but can\u2019t really recall anything about Dallas/Forth Worth (Having only passed through). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T14:32:03-08:00","id":1556729,"title":"","content":"I note that you can get local input into a sourcebook, and still end up with a product which is somewhat out of touch with a particular location. Two of the three authors of <i>London by Night </i>were from London, and it still read like it was written by people whose primary contact with the city was watching <i>Mary Poppins.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T17:19:32-08:00","id":1556733,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know much about Texas, but this definitely sounds like something I\u2019d buy on Storyteller\u2019s Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T01:48:29-08:00","id":1556751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556733#post1556733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know much about Texas, but this definitely sounds like something I\u2019d buy on Storyteller\u2019s Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the amount of effort people put into thinking about / discussing these ideas, it would be relatively straightforward to take that one step further and create a book for the Storyteller\u2019s Vault. There\u2019s a decent market for quality products, and it does encourage interest in the game.<br /> <br /> (A few years ago I did have some thoughts about how a series of books for the Vaults systematically covering different American states would be worthwhile. It would take quite a few people to do effectively\u2026)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T13:02:53-08:00","id":1556762,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d suggest that cover each and every State might get a trifle repetitious past a certain point - perhaps going by regions (New England, Mid-Atlantic, Upper South) could be the way to go?<br /> <br /> It is interesting to wonder which \u2018Splats\u2019 would best suit the individual regions and sub-regions of the USA (I know there\u2019s at least one contributor to these forums who\u2019d dearly love to bring out a RAGE ACROSS THE BERING/RAGE ACROSS ALASKA sourcebook).<br /> <br /> Oh, and we can all agree that Florida is Absolutely CHANGELING: THE DREAMING territory, yes? (Actually, now it occurs to me that a \u2018Necropolis\u2019 sourcebook for the Chesapeake Bay Area would be a other potential goer, given it\u2019s history in the American War of Independence, War of 1812 and US Civil War: I suspect that \u2018NECROPOLIS: ARLINGTON\u2019 wouod be asking for trouble though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T13:52:07-08:00","id":1556763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556762#post1556762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d suggest that cover each and every State might get a trifle repetitious past a certain point - perhaps going by regions (New England, Mid-Atlantic, Upper South) could be the way to go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would quite firmly disagree with this. One of the key problems with <i>Vampire, </i>particularly in later editions, is the dominance of what might be called \u201cgeneric city by night\u201d. We have the notion of the pompous Ventrue prince, rebellious Brujah rebelling, sneaky Nosferatu spies in the sewers spying, and so on. But look at the early location sourcebooks for <i>Vampire</i> and you see far more variety and creativity than what is now represented in the core rulebooks, partIcularly in V5. A good location sourcebook should represent specificity and depth in representing facets of a game world. The World of Darkness has existed for more than thirty years, and, even just working on pre-existing material, there are an incredible number of different domains which one could use to explore different aspects of the <i>Vampire </i>world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T15:33:02-08:00","id":1556766,"title":"","content":"I always felt like at least one city in Texas should have a Gangrel prince. And not the stereotypical outlaw drifter or noble savage Gangrel, but some sort of ruthless political animal like Ian McShane in Deadwood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T21:41:09-08:00","id":1556775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556762#post1556762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d suggest that cover each and every State might get a trifle repetitious past a certain point - perhaps going by regions (New England, Mid-Atlantic, Upper South) could be the way to go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a>.<br /> <br /> Doing the 50 states wouldn't just be an opportunity to better describe the distinctions of each area, which are many and worthwhile on their own.<br /> <br /> More importantly, even, it would be an opportunity to do what WW couldn't at the time and explore how the fictional elements may vary, show how splats in different locations face distinct problems and find distinct solutions even to similar problems. As I said in another thread, we have a very, <i>very</i> big problem with four particular books, not because they're bad (although lack of locals and all that, they're quite messed up), but because they became staples for things that were supposed to not have a standard. A lot of how people think a Vampire city works isn't what's on the core books (especially the first two editions), but those four specific structures, rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think dedicating each place to a main splat is a good idea. Every splats is everywhere from their respective perspectives, they don't usually limit each-other's presence even when they're not on good terms, as they spend most of their time hiding from each other. A state book may not have every splat cited, but should try to cover some bases and be clear that each one is, for their own account, the masters of the area. Or, if not, for quite specific reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T06:07:09-08:00","id":1556787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556762#post1556762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is interesting to wonder which \u2018Splats\u2019 would best suit the individual regions and sub-regions of the USA (I know there\u2019s at least one contributor to these forums who\u2019d dearly love to bring out a RAGE ACROSS THE BERING/RAGE ACROSS ALASKA sourcebook).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been surprised that Rage Across Alaska wasn't Werewolf's second regional sourcebook back in 92 or 93. Besides the fact that it is vast swath of wilderness (almost the antithesis of NYC), had a native wolf population, was famously connected to the petroleum industry (among others), and a diversity of indigenous cultures, at the time the culling of the state's wolf population and environmentalist protests against it was something that made national news (if only briefly). I think it would have been interesting to see an area were the Red Talons and Wendigo were the most dominant Tribes, making up maybe half the population and getting to control the most powerful Septs/Caerns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556762#post1556762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and we can all agree that Florida is Absolutely CHANGELING: THE DREAMING territory, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Northern part of Florida has always essentially been an extension of the Deep South. The lower portion, especially Miami, is a unique mix of that with the Caribbean and Northeast transplants.<br /> <br /> The Miami of the 80s is almost tailor made for Vampire (especially if you want to do something where current events provide excellent cover for violent confrontations between the Camarilla, Sabbat, and other factions).<br /> <br /> If you have never read any of Carl Hiaasen's novels, they are an excellent blend of environmental issues, local cultures (including the Seminole), and regional weirdness that will make you want to run a Werewolf game in southern Florida.<br /> <br /> Then there is Orlando and the noticeable presence of Walt Disney World. LA by Night flat out presented Disneyland in CA as the creation of the Technocracy, so WDW - which started its life as plans for a scientifically designed utopian &quot;town of the future&quot;- would probably be that by an order of magnitude.<br /> <br /> But yes, there is a lot of Changeling potential, especially in Miami.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556762#post1556762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Actually, now it occurs to me that a \u2018Necropolis\u2019 sourcebook for the Chesapeake Bay Area would be a other potential goer, given it\u2019s history in the American War of Independence, War of 1812 and US Civil War: I suspect that \u2018NECROPOLIS: ARLINGTON\u2019 wouod be asking for trouble though).</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Richard Dansky's short list of Necropolis books he would have liked to do if it had been financially feasible included Boston and Baltimore.<br /> <br /> Arlington would probably be considered part of the greater DC necropolis. The National cemetery would probably be one of the strongest Hierarchy citadels in North America. (DC by Night mentions that Giovanni aren't allowed near it out of fear of potential wraith reactions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:36:45-08:00","id":1556800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556766#post1556766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt like at least one city in Texas should have a Gangrel prince. And not the stereotypical outlaw drifter or noble savage Gangrel, but some sort of ruthless political animal like Ian McShane in Deadwood.</div> </div> </div> </div> This sounds like a potential Robert E. Howard homage in the making - perhaps somebody on the Anarch end of things looking to bring the Movement into a Lone Star State (or consolidate it\u2019s position there) and parlaying some sort of expertise or distinguished history (of tackling Setites?) into ensuring that their assertion of Praxis is respected?<br /> <br /> Perhaps somebody in the early 20th century boxing game (Which has always been rife with intrigue &amp; politicking, not to mention frequently-itinerant) who got caught up in a very different sort of fight?<br /> <br /> <br /> My first mental image was of Mr John Brolin, but it further occurred to me that Mr Vincent Donfrio had played Robert E. Howard, the Kingpin of Crime AND a rather scary mountain man, so he\u2019d be another strong pick.<br /> <br /> In any case, I believe the strong tradition of boxing as a poor man\u2019s way out of the gutter would make it an excellent source of physically-imposing recruits to the Kindred (Whether as ghouls or vampires), so it might be interesting to show a Texas vampire making efforts to corner the market.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:43:33-08:00","id":1556802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it would have been interesting to see an area were the Red Talons and Wendigo were the most dominant Tribes, making up maybe half the population and getting to control the most powerful Septs/Caerns. </div> </div> </div> I quite agree: One suspects that there would also be a considerable number of \u2018guest crusaders\u2019 doing their bit to help defend \u2018The Last Frontier\u2019 (or just enjoy a glimpse into the Good Old Days, despite the Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, there is a lot of Changeling potential, especially in Miami. </div> </div> </div> Any state that produces the \u2018Florida Man\u2019 phenomenon is one where those who prefer reality to be an option, rather than a positive obligation, can thrive (and that\u2019s before we get into the illusive glamour of the tourist industry).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arlington would probably be considered part of the greater DC necropolis. The National cemetery would probably be one of the strongest Hierarchy citadels in North America. (DC by Night mentions that Giovanni aren't allowed near it out of fear of potential wraith reactions.) </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s always nice to see the Giovanni reminded that they\u2019re mere necromancers, not uncrowned Kings of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:46:37-08:00","id":1556803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556729#post1556729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that you can get local input into a sourcebook, and still end up with a product which is somewhat out of touch with a particular location. Two of the three authors of <i>London by Night </i>were from London, and it still read like it was written by people whose primary contact with the city was watching <i>Mary Poppins.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> The problem, I suppose, is that familiarity with London does not necessarily equate to familiarity with <i>Victorian</i> London.<br /> <br /> I mean come on, any Victorian Age Vampire sourcebook that does not start with some variation on \u201cThe sun never sets on the British Empire because not even the Almighty could trust those people in the dark\u201d is just leaving money on the table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:58:38-08:00","id":1556804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556775#post1556775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a>.<br /> <br /> Doing the 50 states wouldn't just be an opportunity to better describe the distinctions of each area, which are many and worthwhile on their own.<br /> <br /> More importantly, even, it would be an opportunity to do what WW couldn't at the time and explore how the fictional elements may vary, show how splats in different locations face distinct problems and find distinct solutions even to similar problems. As I said in another thread, we have a very, <i>very</i> big problem with four particular books, not because they're bad (although lack of locals and all that, they're quite messed up), but because they became staples for things that were supposed to not have a standard. A lot of how people think a Vampire city works isn't what's on the core books (especially the first two editions), but those four specific structures, rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think dedicating each place to a main splat is a good idea. Every splats is everywhere from their respective perspectives, they don't usually limit each-other's presence even when they're not on good terms, as they spend most of their time hiding from each other. A state book may not have every splat cited, but should try to cover some bases and be clear that each one is, for their own account, the masters of the area. Or, if not, for quite specific reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> My concern is that by trying over every single state for every single \u2018splat\u2019 this project would risk spreading itself too thin trying to cover absolutely <i>everything</i> from every angle.<br /> <br /> To my mind the best way to keep things interesting for the reader without placing too much of a burden on the writers would be to assign each state to the most suitable splat and then include just enough on other lines for interested parties to spin up their own ideas on the subject.<br /> <br /> Remember, a good sourcebook is all about suggesting possibilities, rather than presenting the most complete picture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T18:17:21-08:00","id":1556818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556804#post1556804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, a good sourcebook is all about suggesting possibilities, rather than presenting the most complete picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that the main quality of a good sourcebook is a high utility value. This represents high usability for the reader, where the sourcebook completes work for the reader. A good example is the first edition of <i>Chicago by Night,</i> which could be used as plug-and-play module in a game; a Storyteller could read once, and then throw the players into this environment with almost no additional preparation beyond a basic idea of the framework of a chronicle. Conversely, an example of a book with low utility value (and we will go for a location sourcebook, because of the subject of the thread) is <i>Iberia by Night. </i>It\u2019s not a badly written book in a technical sense, but has so little detail on the fundamentals that it barely helps with chronicle preparation. If I\u2019m going to have to source some maps, generate the NPCs, work out the big background dynamics, and so on, it\u2019s barely worth picking up the book; I may as well make everything up from scratch.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T23:57:05-08:00","id":1556826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556804#post1556804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern is that by trying over every single state for every single \u2018splat\u2019 this project would risk spreading itself too thin trying to cover absolutely <i>everything</i> from every angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>'This project' right now is just Lone Star by Night. The idea is to make Texas.<br /> <br /> As far as picturing future projects is worthwhile, we're arguing <b><i>models</i></b> for sourcebooks, not really organizing a bunch of randoms, some of whom who aren't even from the North American continent and would prefer to devote such amount of effort into doing their own countries, to try the huge commitment of covering the whole US in a systematic, concerted effort.<br /> <br /> Lone Star by Night is already plenty of work being just Texas from a Vampire perspective. If it really get done, it'll serve as a model for the next person who decides they either want to make a new state or to expand splats covered in Texas, something that person will be whom decides.<br /> <br /> Making <i><b>this one book</b></i>, as far as we can even say it will be a book, to cover all splats, though, that perfectly feasible. Next time we see when next time comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T11:46:37-08:00","id":1556838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556358#post1556358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had half-remembered that Meerlinda was stationed in Texas, thanks for reminding us of this. In that vein, with a major Tremere hub in Texas, part of me is tempted to use that to do a sort of Cyclonopedia (by Reza Negarestani) style thing. For those not familiar, Cyclonopedia is a work of CCRU-inflected \u201ctheory fiction\u201d, a sort of creative pseudo-non-fiction or ARG kinda work that posits Oil as a psuedo-sentient entity which is actively using human beings to foster its own ends of recreating a planet-state resembling the ultra-tropical period of its dinosaur-composition lived. It\u2019s kind of cybernetics mixed with the Living Oil subplot from the X-Files. I think it\u2019s probably too esoteric to be a central plot point but maybe a sort of background mystery that could serve as a crossover for Vampire/Werewolf/Mage, reminiscent of the White Worm in Vienna or the Tumor under NYC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to be asinine on this, but the actual composition of petroleum and coal is a little more convoluted. But minor nitpickery, the base premise could be valid for a chronicle and involve alien, dead/metamorphosed being much, much older than dinossaurs.<br /> <br /> (What brings up the nice detail that coal being a form of carbon in crystaline form could have all sort of circuitous processes going on under our noses behind the morass of a bunch of other things)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556358#post1556358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Texas, it also gets to do Southern Gothic, primarily in the east. Robert E Howard did several horror stories set in the ArkLaTex region where the three states meet, with &quot;Pigeons from Hell&quot; being the most famous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love &quot;Pigeons from Hell&quot;, so heartily approve of the suggestion. Damn, one could even play with some of Howard's stories from other places with a bit of relocalization like Fire of Ashurbanipal (rumored pre-columbian ruined city) or Shadow Kingdom (reptilian conspiracy?setites? Yes)<br /> <br /> Was also going to cite the subterranean realm\u200b of K'n-yan\u200b from Lovecraft's the Mound, but it looks like that is actually set in Oklahoma\u200b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T12:10:17-08:00","id":1556839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556766#post1556766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt like at least one city in Texas should have a Gangrel prince. And not the stereotypical outlaw drifter or noble savage Gangrel, but some sort of ruthless political animal like Ian McShane in Deadwood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Al Swearengen is my all-time favorite television character, so I would be all for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T18:49:01-08:00","id":1556870,"title":"","content":"Don't know if anyone has brought up already, but the Houston metropolitan area happens to have a number of quite significant ports - Houston, Corpus Christi, Beaumont, Freeport, Galveston, Texas City, and Port Arthur, among others - on the Gulf of Mexico, that can make a venue for interactions with people, kindred or other supernaturals from states, north american or mexican, of the gulf coast and even Cuba. Centuries, if not millenia when one goes into pre-columbian trade, of crosspolination, disputes, migrations and mostly forgotten alliances, rivalries or treats.<br /> <br /> Things like Modius going from labor-connected rival of Lodin in Chicago to prince of Gary, that would go from major steel producing center to borderline ghost town in their decades of disputes or Quentin King projecting influence of his court into the whole Boston metro area through his &quot;Six Knights&quot; brood siblings, or back to Gary, Lucian self-exiling from Chicago but still playing a role as power in smugling networks all across the Great Lakes from the apparently crumbling city, away from even most kindred notice as he much prefers, come to mind as possible examples of scenarios for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-20-2025, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T14:31:22-08:00","id":1556878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556870#post1556870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I love &quot;Pigeons from Hell&quot;, so heartily approve of the suggestion. Damn, one could even play with some of Howard's stories from other places with a bit of relocalization like Fire of Ashurbanipal (rumored pre-columbian ruined city) or Shadow Kingdom (reptilian conspiracy?setites? Yes)<br /> <br /> Was also going to cite the subterranean realm of K'n-yan\u200b from Lovecraft's the Mound, but it looks like that is actually set in Oklahoma\u200b.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve gotta check out this \u201cPigeons From Hell\u201d story it sounds like! Ruined pre-Columbian city might fit better a bit north around the area of Cahokia or perhaps a bit further west around the area of the historical Pueblo or Cliff Dwellers. <br /> <br /> That said, doing something with Shadow Kingdom and its conspiracy, including a Settite connection could def be interesting. Particularly in the context of the 80s Texas Counter-Culture, particularly important if we assume an early 90s start-date, where you\u2019ve got everything from Discordians and Church of the SubGenius guys running around doing culture-jamming stuff to take inspo from. A quick check tells me the CotSG guy (Ivan Stang; look up a picture of him, he\u2019s got a classic look for this archetype) is from Dallas which synchronizes well with the central position of Deley Plaza in the mythos.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note while \u201891 would be prior to Alex Jones getting his own Austin public broadcast show or the events of Waco or Oklahoma City, you still have a bubbling conspiracy-right underground bubbling with a mixture of old John Birch era tracts, 80s UFOlogy mythos from the likes of Bill Cooper, and post-Iran Contra early internet message boards (especially heating up with Poppy Bush at the helm of the Gulf War and the \u2018New World Order\u2019 speech from 1990) and a historic link to the long tradition of radical right militias and paramilitaries in the southwest going back to the Minutemen (and possibly the splinter Secret Army Organization) of the 1960s.<br /> <br /> That said the connection to Texas with Oklahoma alongside the larger southwest and southeast is something of note to consider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556870#post1556870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't know if anyone has brought up already, but the Houston metropolitan area happens to have a number of quite significant ports - Houston, Corpus Christi, Beaumont, Freeport, Galveston, Texas City, and Port Arthur, among others - on the Gulf of Mexico, that can make a venue for interactions with people, kindred or other supernaturals from states, north american or mexican, of the gulf coast and even Cuba. Centuries, if not millenia when one goes into pre-columbian trade, of crosspolination, disputes, migrations and mostly forgotten alliances, rivalries or treats.<br /> <br /> Things like Modius going from labor-connected rival of Lodin in Chicago to prince of Gary, that would go from major steel producing center to borderline ghost town in their decades of disputes or Quentin King projecting influence of his court into the whole Boston metro area through his &quot;Six Knights&quot; brood siblings, or back to Gary, Lucian self-exiling from Chicago but still playing a role as power in smugling networks all across the Great Lakes from the apparently crumbling city, away from even most kindred notice as he much prefers, come to mind as possible examples of scenarios for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh 100%, my greatest amount of personal experience with Texas is visiting Houston a few times so it\u2019s at the forefront of my mind. It\u2019s a crossroads between the Texas Triangle &amp; Gulf Coast megalopolis so naturally it\u2019s quite important, plus somewhat absorbing the role Galveston once had as a major Texas city in port prior to the Hurricane of 1900. For the whole Gulf Coast region of the 20th century really, the echoes of the Cuban Revolution is something that has to be addressed.<br /> <br /> I definitely think that the dominant vampiric power in Houston has to be a major influence, although perhaps a relative latercomer like Texas as a whole (plus Galveston again).<br /> <br /> The idea I keep playing with in my mind is building from the idea of the Texas Camarilla being the young turks seeking to outflank Lodin\u2019s position from Chicago in the mid-century and probably getting the blessing from sect movers and shakers sometimes in the 1960s (or earlier if we backdate the Anarch Revolt), with Lodin simultaneously earning a lot of respect and leverage for halting the Anarch Revolt\u2019s eastward expansion and minimizing the extent of Sabbat incursions in the Midwest (despite the loss of Detroit; I don\u2019t know when it fell in canon but IMO it ought to be around this time) but also getting mired in perennial battles with a Midwestern anarch movement that was never fully uprooted (see the Council Wars of the 80s and so on). In contrast, Texas and the other southwestern/sun belt princes emerge as a new power in the North American Camarilla through the use of avant-garde tactics to keep the Anarchs on the run (and of course being married to the clique of political and economic interests rising in the region).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T15:38:19-08:00","id":1556880,"title":"","content":"Well, for starters i would like to point out that Veracruz, the city once ruled by <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eletria\" target=\"_blank\">Eletria </a>- and now possibly under the aegis of Lodin's sire Datura - is among the major cities on the mexican side of the Gulf Coast. The state of Yucatan, where possibly stands the ruined pre-columbian city of Tzental and the ancient known as &quot;<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mictlantecuhtli_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">the Wanderer</a>&quot;, too.<br /> <br /> No doubt if one cares to delve some more in the wiki or PDFs to mine, a bunch of entertaining easter eggs and possible &quot;family relations&quot; to pick and mess with for one's own NPCs will crop up and open room for all kinds of cross-regional plots with it. And that without even going into the state's and its history proper yet.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems Houston played a significant role in the cotton and slave trade, though not to the same degree as New Orleans.<br /> So connections with both that city and/or the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Southern_Lords\" target=\"_blank\">Southron Lords</a> is another potential hook for complications.<br /> <br /> (Or go with a twist by having the prince or a primogen be the disgruntled slave-childe that turned upon his ancient sire. The city going through a borderline anarch uprising through the Civil War - but since it wasn't really Camarilla up to that point, diplomatic heads just swept details under the rug and welcomed the new local rulers of the night into the sect with open arms. Stream of consciousness idea, no idea how appropriate or not would it be to Houston or nearby cities actual history in the period)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-21-2025, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T17:44:57-08:00","id":1556943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556317-notes-towards-a-\u2018lone-star-by-night\u2019?p=1556878#post1556878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while \u201891 would be prior to Alex Jones getting his own Austin public broadcast show</div> </div> </div> </div>At that time, Alex Jones was still known as Bill Hicks. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}